            ("What happens to Earth's rocky crust under towering continental glaciers?", ["Massive ice weight depresses crustal rock slowly downward into the pliant mantle.", "Freezing ground freezes deep mantle magma completely solid.", "Mountain peaks crack violently straight upward under snow loads.", "Ocean currents push coastal cliffs inward by forty kilometers."], 0, "ITP-MOD-02", "B2", "Massa es raksasa menekan kerak bumi melesak ke mantel lunak di bawahnya."),
            ("What geological phenomenon is called 'post-glacial rebound'?", ["The gradual upward rise of crust after thick ice loads melt away.", "Sudden volcanic mudslides rushing through dry valley troughs.", "Glacial boulders bouncing downhill during steep spring thaws.", "Winter sea ice colliding repeatedly against fjord walls."], 0, "ITP-MOD-02", "B1", "Pelentingan ke atas kerak bumi setelah beban es mencair hilang."),
