            ("Physically, how do owl trailing-edge fringes suppress audible flight noise?", ["They fracture large thunderous air swirls into gentle tiny silent vortices.", "They glue swirling air molecules motionless atop wingtips.", "They generate opposing sound pitches canceling low frequencies out.", "They raise air density cleanly below owl bellies."], 0, "ITP-MOD-02", "B2", "Rumbai memecah pusaran besar bising menjadi pusaran mikro jauh lebih senyap."),
